2026-06-17 ~16:00 PT — ADR-072 filed v0.1 (Architect) — Skill-Routing Architecture (fluid model + defense-in-depth). Authored from the grounding substrate (`dev/active/adr-072-grounding-findings-2026-06-17.md`) — PIPER.md + SKILL.md formats + native SKILLS.md + pre_classifier.py read FIRST per the grounding-first trigger (don't draft from speculation). PM escalated priority (PA relay): wanted it now, not Thu/Fri. The 5 ratification decisions: D1 — Layer-4 native authoritative / Layer-2 plugin pre-classifier authoritative (additive layers, highest-confidence-fired wins, floor catches all); D2 — `PIPER-SKILLS.md` manifest DERIVED from SKILL.md frontmatter (ADR-059-by-construction, not hand-kept); D3 — `ask_piper` routes-within + `run_skill(name)` meta-tool (NOT per-skill tools; no rename, m-40); D4 — static registry derived at server start + SKILL.md procedure injection (ADR-066 D7 server-owned; #1245 build target); D5 — Trust Gradient as a separate permission layer above routing (should-we vs which-one) — PENDING CXO + HOST trust-lens. Load-bearing mechanism: derive routing metadata from SKILL.md frontmatter (one source → manifest + Layer-2 patterns + Layer-1 descriptions), curing hand-maintained-index rot (the stale native SKILLS.md is a live Pattern-073; #1106 MANIFEST-derive is the precedent; m-41 mechanism-displaces-vigilance). Unblocks Wave P + #1245. D1–D4 Arch-ratifiable in-lane; D5 pending trust-lens before any proactive-surfacing ships. — Arch

2026-06-17 ~19:00 PT — ADR-072 → v0.2 ACCEPTED (Architect); D5 RATIFIED with CXO + HOST trust-lens folded. Both reviewers aligned. CXO: the gradient gates **Piper-initiated** (proactive surfacing / autonomous action), **never user-reaching-for-their-own** (user-invoked execution / viewing own data) — "ratify if D5 gates proactive not user-invoked"; it does. HOST: separation is load-bearing (keep); substantiability/fail-closed right (keep); + TWO refinements folded — (1) **consequential-action carve-out**: reactive (user-asked) is tier-independent only for *information* skills; skills with side-effects (modify state / send external / spend credits / hard-to-reverse) are tier-gated even when reactive (the tier = account authorization for that action *class*); discriminator = side-effects, not who-initiated; named now before the first consequential skill ships (m-36); (2) **transparency-when-gated**: when the Gradient gates a proactive proposal, surface that the gate exists (via trust-check), not silence — silent non-action is itself a trust gap. Whole ADR D1–D5 now ratified; Wave P fully unblocked (incl. proactive-surfacing rules). — Arch

2026-06-18 ~08:00 PT — Duty-cycle STOP rubric softened for sentinel-present-but-content-complete cases. PM-ratified. Context: Web's June 17 session log had a complete Day-close handoff section (cron re-armed, queue state documented, work on main, 21:52 timestamp) but was missing the canonical `<!-- DAY-CLOSED: YYYY-MM-DD -->` marker. Docs patched it + sent memo to Web. PM asked whether the rubric should be softened. Decision: sentinel remains required (machine-detectable close-out; keeps grep-based detection intact). Softer behavior for detection heuristics: (1) START Step-0 self-heal — if sentinel is absent but log contains a "Day-close handoff" section, treat as "soft close": warn in the self-heal output but skip the full retroactive close-out pass; (2) Docs merge-keeper sweep — note the gap but do not flag as "potentially stranded work" if git shows main was clean at that timestamp. The sentinel is not optional — Web's memo stands — but the consequence of a missing sentinel is graduated: warn on soft-close, full retroactive pass only on genuinely unclosed sessions. Skill updates needed: duty-cycle-tick STOP section (soft-close detection) + START Step-0 self-heal. — Docs

2026-06-18 ~17:35 PT — #1283 action↔handler routing-integrity audit SCOPED (Arch, PM-directed; scope memo to Lead cc PM/PA). Root cause: action names are free strings with NO canonical source — the classifier emits a free-text `"action"` (no enum constrains it), the prompt vocabulary is just few-shot examples (~18 in prompts.py), and the rail aliases are a third hand-maintained list (~50 in workflow_entries.py); overlap=2; the LLM emits a 51st (`get_project_status`, conf 1.0 — the #1269 fabrication). DECISIONS: (1) **SoT = the dispatch registration is canonical; DERIVE the classifier prompt's action vocabulary from it** (derive-don't-maintain — m-41, same mechanism as ADR-072 SKILL.md-frontmatter-derive + #1106 MANIFEST-derive) → collapses dead-registration + name-drift by construction; type via an `Action` registry/enum. (2) **Runtime-safety nuance (ADR-060 floor-first refinement)**: a high-confidence ACTION with no registered handler must NOT silently floor-improvise (the #1269 fabrication mechanism) — log it (the mode-4 signal) + clarify/honest-degrade, not fabricate. (3) **Enforcement = TWO altitudes**: (A) static reachability lint, every-commit, deterministic (baseline-ratchet shape like token-lint / the dispatch-site ratchet; in `test_architecture_enforcement.py`) asserting every action is handler-reachable = rail ∪ category ∪ intentional-floor → catches modes 1/2/3; (B) behavioral golden-corpus suite on the canonical-retest harness (real LLM, gated cadence) → catches mode 4 (undocumented emission). (4) **Probe = container-init production path**; reachability = **rail ∪ category ∪ intentional-floor** (the false-positive guard for category-routed actions — "off-rail ≠ unreachable"). Refines ADR-059 (capability-accuracy → runtime action-reachability) + ADR-060 (floor-fall guard). **ADR-073 candidate** once the clean probe validates. Lead runs the clean probe + implements fixes + the static lint; Arch co-owns the enforcement design + ratifies. Pattern-073 instance (prompt-vs-rail drift); m-30 (behavioral probe = consumer-trace). — Arch

