2026-07-01 ~15:40 PT — #1342 + #1231 connector-framework boundaries (Arch ruling, Lead building). Principle: adjacent intent-layer boundaries SHARE #1232's Connector-protocol vocabularies but do NOT extend its 4-method protocol (ADR-070 D2, applied twice). (1) **#1342 target-resolution** = a SEPARATE resolution service (services/integrations/resolution/), NOT a 5th Connector method — target-selection-from-Piper-config is a different altitude than the protocol's resource-resolve. `ResolvedTarget = {source: ResolutionSource, connector, payload}`; promote the already-connector-agnostic `ResolutionSource` as-is; `ResolvedRepo` = GitHub payload; design-for-calendar-on-paper, build-GitHub-only (m-40). (2) **#1231 honest-degrade** = unify the VOCABULARY: metadata layer carries the same `DegradationReason` enum the adapter emits (share currency, not container). Added `DegradationReason.NOT_CONFIGURED` (onboard gap, distinct from CONNECT_REQUIRED reconnect gap — Lead+Arch agreed; real UX distinction). Reason→copy = ONE shared policy (services/intent_service/degradation_copy.py, generalizes calendar_offer_policy) — CXO voice-passes once, HOST trust lens (ADR-072 D5 transparency-when-gated). Connector-level degrade surfaces once-per-response; item-level/partial = per-item. No new ADR for either; recorded here under the ADR-070 family. — Lead (ruling: Arch)
